{
    "_comment": "The mobile editor's Locations screen (EditorMobileLocationsScreen), from the right panel's locations button once the map is tracked: Create New Location - a name, then the origin placed in the scene - and the dimension's locations nearest first, each a framed row a tap on anywhere of selects to edit. Sizes in UI points: 1000 across the screen. The window has a fixed height and scrolls, so everything above the list and the list itself say flexShrink 0: yoga's web defaults let a fixed-height window shrink its children to fit, and over nineteen rows the Create button came out 40 points tall. The right padding leaves the phone's 70-pixel scrollbar room beside the rows rather than over them.",
    "?_ignore_": [
        { "condition": {"type": "platform", "value": "Mobile"}, "value": false },
        { "condition": "", "value": true }
    ],

    "_comment2": "Not modal: the name prompt is a modal of the app's, and two modals in the one on-screen ImGui context close each other every frame.",
